<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eleanor of England, Queen of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1162">1162</a>–<a href="/years/1214">1214</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Leonor of England</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eleanor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> was a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine">Eleanor of Aquitaine</a> who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-viii">Alfonso VIII</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> in 1177. She was a patron of religious houses, including the royal convent of Las Huelgas at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a>, and of troubadours. Her children included Berengaria, later queen of Castile, Henry I of Castile and Blanche, queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. She died a few weeks after her husband in 1214.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-england-queen-of-castile.jpg" alt="Eleanor of England, Queen of Castile" width="186" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EleonoraAngl.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
